================================================================================
SECTION 1: PROJECT ROADMAP & STRUCTURE
================================================================================
Every project MUST include these deliverables in this exact order:

1. AIM
    - One-sentence mission statement
    - Problem statement (what pain does this solve?)
    - Target audience
    - Success criteria (measurable outcomes)

2. INPUT / OUTPUT SPECIFICATION
    - INPUT: Data formats, API endpoints, user interactions, file types, 
      environment variables, config schemas
    - OUTPUT: Screens, API responses, files generated, reports, notifications
    - EDGE CASES: Empty inputs, malformed data, timeout scenarios, 
      rate limiting, concurrent access

3. WORKING MECHANISM
    - Data flow diagram (textual or Mermaid)
    - State machine description
    - Algorithm overview (complexity: time/space)
    - Concurrency model (threads, async, actors, channels)
    - Error handling strategy (fail-fast vs graceful degradation)

4. TECH-STACK (Justified Selection)
    - Frontend: [Framework + State Management + Styling + Build Tool]
      * Justify: Why this over alternatives? Performance? Ecosystem? Team?
    - Backend: [Runtime + Framework + ORM/DB Driver + Middleware]
      * Justify: Scalability? Type safety? Throughput?
    - Database: [Primary + Cache + Search + Queue]
      * Justify: ACID needs? Read/write ratio? Latency requirements?
    - DevOps: [Container + Orchestration + CI/CD + Monitoring]
      * Justify: Deployment frequency? Rollback strategy?
    - AI/ML (if applicable): [Model + Framework + Vector DB + Inference]
      * Justify: Accuracy vs latency trade-off? Fine-tuning needs?

5. SYSTEM ARCHITECTURE
    - Layered diagram: Presentation → Business Logic → Data Access → External
    - Microservices vs Monolith (justify with pros/cons table)
    - API Gateway pattern, Circuit Breaker, Bulkhead, Retry policies
    - Database schema (ER diagram in textual form)
    - Caching strategy (Redis layers, CDN, browser cache headers)
    - Message queue architecture (events, pub/sub, sagas)

6. ADVANTAGES & DIFFERENTIATORS
    - Performance benchmarks (target: &lt;100ms API response, &lt;2s LCP)
    - Security advantages (auth flow, encryption at rest/transit)
    - Scalability path (horizontal scaling, sharding, read replicas)
    - Developer experience (hot reload, type safety, debugging tools)

